## Finding

`crime_00070` — `duplicate_component_shape`, confidence 0.70. A `<div>` subtree (hash `e96b55b64336…`) repeats verbatim across 4 files: the invoice form's footer row (flex container holding a "Cancel" link back to `/dashboard/invoices` plus a submit `<Button>`). The only thing that differs between sites is the submit label ("Create Invoice" vs "Edit Invoice").

## Files that would change

- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` (lines 142–150)
- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` (lines 152–160)
- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` (lines 101–109)
- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` (lines 112–120)

Plus one new file per app: `app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` (or shared inside each variant — these are two independent Next.js examples, so don't try to consolidate across `final-example` and `starter-example`; treat them as two parallel refactors of the same shape).

## Proposed component

`<FormActions>` — a thin presentational footer with one variable label and one variable destination. Keep the surface minimal; this is a 9-line subtree, so over-parameterising it would re-introduce the cost it's meant to remove.

```tsx
// app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';

type FormActionsProps = {
  submitLabel: string;
  cancelHref?: string;        // defaults to /dashboard/invoices
  cancelLabel?: string;       // defaults to "Cancel"
};

export function FormActions({
  submitLabel,
  cancelHref = '/dashboard/invoices',
  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',
}: FormActionsProps) {
  return (
    <div className="mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4">
      <Link
        href={cancelHref}
        className="flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200"
      >
        {cancelLabel}
      </Link>
      <Button type="submit">{submitLabel}</Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Public API

- **Props:** `submitLabel: string` (required), `cancelHref?: string`, `cancelLabel?: string`.
- **Slots:** none. The two call sites only vary by label text, so a single `submitLabel` prop is cheaper than a `children`/`actions` slot. If a future caller needs a destructive button or a third action, promote `actions` to a slot at that point — not pre-emptively.

### Call sites become

```tsx
<FormActions submitLabel="Create Invoice" />
<FormActions submitLabel="Edit Invoice" />
```

## What I deliberately did **not** parameterise

- The container classes (`mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4`) — those are the *shape*; making them a prop defeats the extraction.
- The Cancel button styling — same reason; if it needs to change later, change it in `FormActions`.
- A `variant="create" | "edit"` enum — the label is the only difference; an enum would re-encode it indirectly.

The `duplicated_role_status_plan_check` findings (`crime_00071`/`crime_00072`, "pending"/"paid" checks scattered across the same forms + `status.tsx`) are a separate, larger refactor — leave them out of this change.
